## Files

| file | what it does |
|---|---|
| `t3.py` | `a [procs]`: T3a at x = 10⁴, 10⁵. `e [procs]`: the x = 10⁶ check, which uses fewer draws and a known bracket. `b [x]`: the T3b profile. `c`: T3c. `s`: the T3b summary across x. All use the kernels of `t1lib.c` through `t1.py`. |
| `make_t3.py` | builds the tables above from the JSON files |
| `t3a.json`, `t3a.txt`, `t3a_x1000000.json`, `t3a_x1000000.txt` | T3a: per-draw thresholds (x = 10⁴, 10⁵; and the x = 10⁶ check) |
| `t3b_x*.json`, `t3b_x*.txt` | T3b: binned profiles, bands in u = ln r/ln x, excess shares below x^θ |
| `t3c.json`, `t3c.txt` | T3c: binned profiles, and the tempered and greedy strikes and the fullest class for each modulus |

Run times: T3a takes 5 minutes on 2 cores (the x = 10⁶ check took 60 minutes on 2 shared cores). T3b takes 1 s at x = 10⁵ and
80 s at 10⁶. T3c takes 1 s.
